      "versionNonce": 100868,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "role": "text"
      },
      "text": "Each cluster has a tainted system pool, an app pool for baseline load, and a burst pool that KEDA scales on queue depth; the burst pool can run on ACI virtual nodes to avoid waiting for node provisioning.\nThe Horizontal Pod Autoscaler scales pods, the Cluster Autoscaler scales nodes, and every node pool spans three availability zones.",
      "originalText": "Each cluster has a tainted system pool, an app pool for baseline load, and a burst pool that KEDA scales on queue depth; the burst pool can run on ACI virtual nodes to avoid waiting for node provisioning.\nThe Horizontal Pod Autoscaler scales pods, the Cluster Autoscaler scales nodes, and every node pool spans three availability zones.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": false
    },
